To determine the maximum score, we need to calculate the total time spent on training and solving problems. The time spent on training is $T/10$ minutes, and the time spent on solving problems is the sum of the difficulty divided by the skill level for each problem. The skill level decreases by $0.1$ after each episode, so we need to adjust the time spent on solving problems accordingly.

We can solve this problem using dynamic programming. We'll create an array dp where dp[i] represents the maximum score achievable up to the i-th problem. We'll iterate over the problems and update the dp array based on the difficulty and skill level of each problem.

