<code>
```python
def last_digit_fibonacci(N):
    if N <= 1:
        return N
    fib_modulo = [0, 1]
    for i in range(2, N + 1):
        fib_modulo.append((fib_modulo[-1] + fib_modulo[-2]) % 10)
    return fib_modulo[-1]
```
</code>
</reasoning>

This code efficiently finds the last digit of the $N$th Fibonacci number using modular arithmetic. It iterates through the Fibonacci sequence modulo 10, storing the last digits in a list. Finally, it returns the last element of the list, which represents the last digit of the $N$th Fibonacci number.

