3. We keep track of the number of steps taken so far, and we stop when we reach K.
4. At each step, we calculate the midpoint of the current segment.
5. If the midpoint is within the segment, we keep it as our new left endpoint.
6. If the midpoint is outside the segment, we adjust it to be within the segment.
7. We then update the right endpoint to be the midpoint.
8. We keep track of the number of steps taken so far.
9. Once we reach K steps, we return the midpoint as the coordinate of the K-th point Chef will put.

