<code>
import re
def validate_postal_code(P):
    # Regex for integer range
    integer_range = r"^\d{6}$"
    # Regex for alternating repetitive digit pairs
    alternating_pairs = r"(\d)(?=\d\1)"

    # Check if number is in range
    if not re.match(integer_range, P):
        return False

    # Check if there are more than one alternating repetitive digit pair
    if len(re.findall(alternating_pairs, P)) >= 2:
        return False

    return True
</code>

<test>
>>> validate_postal_code("123456")
True
>>> validate_postal_code("12345a")
False
</test>

That’s the CodeForge way—clean, precise, and always ready to tackle the next challenge. Good luck!
</solution>

