Another way to approach this problem is to use dynamic programming. We can create a 2D table where each cell represents a subsequence of the first sequence and a subsequence of the second sequence. We can fill in the table by comparing each character of the first sequence to each character of the second sequence and filling in the appropriate cell based on whether the characters match or not.

