For example, if the string is "racecar", we can use recursion to check if it’s a palindrome by comparing "racecar" with "racecar". We can use two pointers to check if the string is a palindrome. One pointer starts at the beginning of the string and the other starts at the end of the string. We move the pointers towards each other until they meet or until we find a mismatch. If we find a mismatch, the string is not a palindrome. If we don’t find a mismatch, the string is a palindrome.

