Next, we need to find the vaulters who cleared that greatest height successfully. This can be done by comparing the strings at that height.
Then, we need to determine who had the fewest unsuccessful attempts at that height. This can be done by counting the X's in the string at that height.
Finally, we need to determine who has the fewest total unsuccessful attempts across all heights. This can be done by summing the X's in all the strings at all heights.
We also need to consider ties. If there are ties for one of the finishing places, we need to break them by tracing backwards through the heights until we find the greatest height that all vaulters cleared successfully. Then, we need to determine who had the fewest unsuccessful attempts at this height.
If there are ties for the first place finish, we need to determine who has the fewest total unsuccessful attempts across all heights.
