For example, in the first case, 'Aa' has fewer characters than any other string. In the second case, 'abc' has fewer characters than any other string.

I will write a function that takes an array of strings and returns the unique string. I will use the `min_by` method to find the string with the least number of characters. I will use the `size` method to count the number of characters in each string. I will use the `join` method to concatenate the characters in each string. I will use the `strip` method to remove leading and trailing spaces from each string.

Here’s my solution:

```python
def find_uniq(arr):
    return min(arr, key=lambda x: len(x.strip()))
```

