Here is the solution:

```python
def process_sequence(sequence):
    squared = [x**2 if x > 0 else x for x in sequence]
    multiplied_by_3 = [x * 3 if (i+1) % 3 == 0 else x for i, x in enumerate(squared)]
    multiplied_by_minus_one = [x * -1 if (i+1) % 5 == 0 else x for i, x in enumerate(multiplied_by_3)]
    return sum(multiplied_by_minus_one)
```

This function takes a sequence of integers and processes it according to the steps provided. It first squares all positive numbers, then multiplies every third number by 3, and finally multiplies every fifth number by -1. The sum of the processed sequence is returned.

