- `^`: Start of the string
- `((I|V?I{0,3}){1,3})`: Matches the units place (I to IX)
- `(IX|IV|V?I{0,3}){1,3}`: Matches the tens place (X to IX)
- `(M){0,4}`: Matches the thousands place (M to M)
- `$`: End of the string

I’ll write a function that uses this Regular Expression to find all valid Roman numerals in an array. Here’s the solution:

```python
import re

def valid_romans(arr):
    pattern = re.compile(r'^((I|V?I{0,3}){1,3})(IX|IV|V?I{0,3}){1,3}(M){0,4}$')
    return [s for s in arr if pattern.match(s)]
```

This solution uses a Regular Expression to match all valid Roman numerals in the array and returns a list of them. I hope you find this solution helpful!
</solution>

